# <type>(<scope>): <description>
#
# Types:
#   feat:     A new feature
#   fix:      A bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Code style changes (formatting, semicolons, etc)
#   refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     Performance improvement
#   test:     Adding or updating tests
#   build:    Build system or external dependency changes
#   ci:       CI configuration changes
#   chore:    Other changes that don't modify src or test files
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Add "BREAKING CHANGE:" in the commit body or "!" after type
#   Example: feat!: remove deprecated API
#
# The version is not derived from the commit type but from the branch name:
#   breaking/... (major), feature/... (minor), fix/... (patch)
#
# Scope examples: protocol, device, ci, deps
